# Shubh runs with none of these set.
#
# The budget, the schedule and the feasibility findings are computed in code, and
# the explanation falls back to the built-in narrative in lib/narrative.ts, which
# is generated from the plan and passes output verification by construction. A
# model adds personalisation and texture, not facts.
#
# Copy to .env.local to configure one.

# --- A hosted model (pick one) ---
# Google Gemini. Keys come in two shapes: AIza… and the newer AQ.… form.
# GEMINI_API_KEY=

# OpenAI.
# OPENAI_API_KEY=

# Anthropic.
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=

# Override the model for whichever provider is selected.
# SHUBH_MODEL=gemini-2.0-flash

# --- An on-device model (takes precedence over the keys above) ---
#
# Set either of these and inference runs locally: nothing a planner types leaves
# the machine. Any OpenAI-compatible server works; Ollama is the usual one.
#
#   ollama serve && ollama pull qwen3:8b
#
# SHUBH_LOCAL_MODEL=qwen3:8b
# SHUBH_LOCAL_BASE_URL=http://localhost:11434/v1
# SHUBH_LOCAL_LABEL=Ollama

# Let a reasoning model think. Off by default: measured on qwen3:8b, thinking
# consumed the entire token budget in the reasoning field and produced zero
# content tokens, so no answer arrived at all.
# SHUBH_LOCAL_THINKING=1
